    "componentStyles": "A playful, warm, accessible multiplayer game for participants using their phones. The supplied route sequence is Lobby → El Camino → El Pedregal → Los Espinos → La Buena Tierra → Podio Final.\n\nThe OpenPencil document has two pages:\n- **Mobile Web**: six 390×844 route artboards, one per game stage.\n- **Wide Web**: six companion 1280×900 compositions, named with the matching stage plus “Wide Web”. These are responsive layout references, not additional game routes.\n\nThe designs show a sample state. Dynamic seed/life counts, player identities and trivia data must be supplied by the game; never treat illustration placeholders as authoritative game data.\n\n- Primary olive: `#556B2F`; deep olive: `#3F4F22`; pale olive surface: `#E9EDDF`.\n- Warm paper background: `#F7F5EB`; surface: `#FFFEFA`; primary text: `#292B22`; muted text: `#696B60`; border: `#DFE1D6`.\n- Seed accent: `#C59A49` for seed counts/rewards. Rust is reserved for thorn/hazard feedback.\n- Use Nunito for display, body and functional text. Keep mobile body copy around 14–16px, essential instructions at least 14px, and captions 11–13px with adequate contrast.\n- Use an 8px spacing rhythm, 16–20px cards, 12px controls, clear selected/focus states, and interactive targets of at least 44×44px.\n- UI copy uses voseo and the terminology from the project brief.\n\n- **Mobile:** stack content in one column; keep the current game surface and its touch action dominant and within easy reach. Preserve board geometry and the vertical drag path.\n- **Wide web:** use the available width to separate primary play from supporting information without changing action order or priority: lobby invite/players; Camino playfield/seed tally; Pedregal grid/instructions; Espinos trail/lives; trivia questions side-by-side; podium winner/ranking.\n- Keep playable targets usable with touch or pointer. Do not stretch small choice controls across unnecessarily wide measures.\n\n- **Lobby:** QR join, participant names/status, and the 2–6 player start condition. Starting routes to `/camino`.\n- **El Camino:** 10 starting seeds; tap birds; do not assign a numeric duration. The surviving seeds continue to the next challenge.\n- **El Pedregal:** 5×5 memory board and 3-second seed preview. The number/positions shown in artboards are illustrative; surviving seeds determine the life count for Los Espinos.\n- **Los Espinos:** drag the sprout to the finish; every thorn collision removes one life; zero lives eliminates. Show the life count as dynamic.\n- **La Buena Tierra:** two multiple-choice questions. Show the supplied outcomes: 0 correct → small/wilted plant; 1 → medium plant; 2 → large, strong plant. Trivia copy/options are placeholders. Do not invent timers, retries, or incorrect-answer behavior. The growth factor is not numerically specified.\n- **Podio Final:** show positions 1–6 and celebrate the highest score. Example participants/rankings are placeholders; do not invent ties or rules for vacant positions. Preserve `surviving seeds × trivia growth factor` without assigning a numeric factor. Podio has no defined player action.\n- Use the lobby and trivia buttons only for the supplied transitions. Do not invent intermediate completion rules or unspecified game behavior.\n\nFinal trivia questions/options, numeric growth multiplier, El Camino duration, incorrect Pedregal-tap behavior, intermediate completion/transition triggers, tie handling, and vacant podium places must remain unspecified until the product brief defines them."
